    "created_at": "2025-11-20T08:40:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-20T08:40:36Z",
    "body": "Instead of introducing a new `fallbackfor` attribute, what about reusing something like `srcset` as can be found on other elements like `img`? The values of this attribute could be URLs tried in order in case of error.\n\nIt looks like the `link` element already has a `imgsrcset` attribute: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLLinkElement/imageSrcset",
